  "prefLabel": "Lab 204.06 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by the Hearing Officer",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-01-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 204.06 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by the Hearing Officer. The hearing officer, upon the motion of any party, or on their own initiative, shall suspend or waive any requirements or limitation imposed by this chapter when the suspension or waiver:\n\n(a) Appears to be lawful; and\n\n(b) Is more likely to promote the just, accurate, and efficient resolution of the pending dispute than adherence to the particular requirement or procedure.\n\nSource. #5041, eff 1-9-91; ss by #5235, eff 9-27-91; amd by #5658, eff 6-28-93; ss by #6631, INTERIM, eff 11-16-97, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6806, eff 7-18-98; ss by #8682, INTERIM, eff 7-15-06, EXPIRED: 1-11-07\n\nNew. #8922-A, eff 7-1-07; ss by #14534, eff 3-12-26",
